# Build-context excludes for `az acr build` / `docker build` (ADP-cm9 follow-up).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it, `COPY web/ ./` in the root Dockerfile pulls
# in web/.env.local -- a gitignored local-dev override that sets
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=false. Vite loads .env.local at higher priority than .env
# in a production build, so that "false" got baked into the DEPLOYED bundle,
# disabling frontend auth while the backend required it -> every API call 401'd
# with no token -> the SPA failed to render -> black screen. `az acr build`
# only auto-excludes .git/.gitignore, NOT arbitrary gitignored files, so the
# exclusion has to be explicit here.
#
# Deliberately conservative: nothing here is read by either Docker stage
# (frontend `npm ci` + `tsc && vite build`, or the python `pip install`), so
# excluding these cannot change build output -- only prevent the leak and
# shrink the upload.

# Local-only env overrides -- MUST never enter a deploy build (the black-screen bug)
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Secrets cache (Postgres/Keycloak admin passwords) -- must never be baked into an image
infra/azure/.secrets/

# Dependencies + prior build output -- rebuilt fresh inside the image
**/node_modules
web/dist
dist/

# VCS + tooling metadata (not needed to build the image)
.git
.gitignore
.github
.beads
.gitnexus
.claude
.codex
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
